Package: lindos-installer
Version: 1.0.0
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Lindos Team <team@lindos.dev>
Depends: lindos-core (>= 1.0.0), python3 (>= 3.10), curl | wget, util-linux, coreutils
Homepage: https://lindos.dev
Description: Lindos installer flow - the heavy work runs while installing
 Lindos installs with Ubiquity in OEM mode: the live session shows nothing but the
 installer, the installer does everything heavy (system updates, drivers, Google
 Chrome, Wine and the game launchers, Flatpak apps) and the first boot only asks for
 an account name, a password and a few personal choices.
 .
 This package holds the two scripts Ubiquity runs: target-config.sh, the target-config
 hook that does the downloading and installing into the new system (time-boxed,
 always exits 0, leaves dpkg clean, records what it did in
 /var/lib/lindos/install-state.json), and finalize.sh, the short success_command
 that arms Ubiquity's oem-config first-boot wizard. extras.json is the union of
 every Mode's extra packages. Nothing here runs on an installed system: the
 package is on the installation medium only and is removed from the new system
 by the installer.
